Package: GMPP
Type: Package
Title: Genomic mating to predict expected progeny genetic values
Version: 1.0.0
Date: 2026-07-07
Authors@R: c( person("Mengjin", "Zhu", email = "zhumengjin@mail.hzau.edu.cn", role = c("cre", "aut", "cph")),
              person("Xiangyu", "Dai", role = "aut"))
Description: Computes expected progeny genetic values for candidate
    parental mating combinations in plant and animal breeding programs.
    The package implements a three-stage genomic mating pipeline: genomic
    relationship matrices are constructed using the VanRaden method, marker
    effects are estimated via genomic best linear unbiased prediction (GBLUP)
    using the 'gaston' package, and expected progeny genetic values are predicted
    by deriving progeny genotype probabilities from parental genotypes and integrating
    marker effects across genome-wide markers. Both additive and dominance effects
    can be modelled, and the framework supports purebred, crossbred, and multi-breed
    mating designs with optional reference populations for marker effect estimation.
